# 4. PROJECT INQUIRY AND QUOTATION SYSTEM

The existing inquiry form will be upgraded into a centralized project inquiry management system.

The current browser localStorage implementation should be replaced with Supabase database storage.

## 4.1 Inquiry Form Fields

### Client Information

- Full Name
- Company Name (optional)
- Email Address
- Contact Number
- Preferred Contact Method

### Project Information

- Project Category
- Project Location
- Estimated Project Budget
- Estimated Floor Area (optional)
- Target Construction Date
- Property Ownership or Project Readiness (optional)
- Project Description / Scope of Work

### Attachments

- Architectural Plans
- Reference Images
- Other Supporting Documents

### Consent

- Privacy Policy acknowledgment
- Consent to the processing of submitted personal information

## 4.2 Inquiry Submission Workflow

1. Visitor completes the inquiry form.
2. Frontend validates the submitted information.
3. Backend validates and processes the submission.
4. Supabase stores the inquiry.
5. System generates a unique inquiry reference number.
6. Email notification is sent to designated MST personnel.
7. Visitor receives a submission confirmation.
8. Authorized administrators review the inquiry.
9. Administrator updates the inquiry status.
10. MST personnel coordinate with the prospective client.

## 4.3 Inquiry Status Management

| Status | Description |
|---|---|
| New | Newly submitted inquiry |
| Under Review | Inquiry is being evaluated |
| Site Inspection | Site inspection is scheduled |
| Quotation Preparation | Preparing BOQ and project estimate |
| Quotation Sent | Proposal has been sent to the client |
| Negotiation | Discussion or revision of the proposal |
| Approved | Client accepted the proposal |
| Declined | Client declined the proposal |
| Completed | Inquiry has resulted in a completed project |

Each status update should record:

- Previous status
- New status
- Updated by
- Date and time
- Optional administrative remarks

## 4.4 Inquiry Reference Tracking

Every submitted inquiry must have a unique reference number.

Example:

`MST-INQ-2026-00001`

The reference number should be generated securely by the backend.

For the initial release, the client can receive this reference through the confirmation email.

A public inquiry tracking page may be introduced later using a secure reference-based access mechanism. It must not expose internal notes or other clients' information.

