# 6. USER ROLES AND ACCESS CONTROL

The administrative dashboard should implement role-based access control.

| Role | Permissions |
|---|---|
| Super Admin | Full system access, user management, configuration |
| Administrator | Manage inquiries, projects, website content, and reports |
| Staff | Access assigned inquiries and authorized records |

### Access Control Requirements

- Only authenticated users can access administrative pages.
- Users can only perform actions allowed by their assigned role.
- Administrative permissions must be checked on the backend.
- Unauthorized users must not be able to access restricted database records.
- Sensitive administrative actions must be recorded in audit logs.

Hiding frontend buttons is not sufficient security. Supabase Row Level Security and appropriate backend authorization must enforce permissions.

