# 7. SUPABASE BACKEND AND DATABASE ARCHITECTURE

Supabase will serve as the backend platform.

### Technology Stack

| Component | Technology |
|---|---|
| Frontend | React 19 |
| Programming Language | TypeScript |
| Build Tool | Vite |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS 4 |
| Backend Platform | Supabase |
| Database | PostgreSQL |
| Authentication | Supabase Auth |
| File Storage | Supabase Storage |
| Server-side Logic | Supabase Edge Functions |
| Development Environment | Local Machine |

## 7.1 Database Tables

The following database structure is recommended.

| Table | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `profiles` | User profiles and assigned roles |
| `inquiries` | Project inquiry submissions |
| `inquiry_notes` | Internal inquiry notes |
| `inquiry_status_history` | Inquiry status records |
| `projects` | Company construction projects |
| `project_images` | Project photographs and galleries |
| `project_updates` | Project progress records |
| `services` | Company service information |
| `team_members` | Engineering team profiles |
| `credentials` | Company certifications and licenses |
| `testimonials` | Approved client testimonials |
| `notifications` | System notifications |
| `audit_logs` | Administrative activity records |

## 7.2 Storage Buckets

Suggested Supabase Storage buckets:

| Bucket | Access |
|---|---|
| `project-images` | Public approved portfolio images |
| `team-photos` | Public approved team photographs |
| `credentials` | Private by default |
| `inquiry-attachments` | Private |
| `project-documents` | Private |

Private files should only be accessible to authorized users through appropriate access policies or temporary signed URLs.

## 7.3 Database Requirements

- Use primary keys and foreign key relationships.
- Add appropriate indexes for frequently searched fields.
- Generate unique inquiry reference numbers.
- Use timestamps for record creation and updates.
- Maintain inquiry status history.
- Validate important fields.
- Use database constraints where appropriate.
- Implement Row Level Security on all exposed tables.
- Restrict administrative functions to authorized users.

## 7.4 Backend Security

- Use Supabase Authentication.
- Implement Row Level Security policies.
- Protect administrative routes.
- Never expose the Supabase service-role key in frontend code.
- Validate uploaded file types and sizes.
- Restrict private document access.
- Implement spam protection and submission rate limiting.
- Protect administrative operations with server-side authorization.
- Maintain database backups and recovery procedures.

