# 13. LOCAL DEVELOPMENT AND ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION

The project will initially run on a local development environment.

### Initial Setup

1. Install Node.js and npm.
2. Open the existing MST project in Visual Studio Code.
3. Install project dependencies.
4. Create and configure the Supabase project.
5. Configure the database schema.
6. Configure environment variables.
7. Run the application locally.
8. Test inquiry submissions and database operations.

### Environment Variables

```env
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=your_supabase_project_url
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_supabase_publishable_key
```

Only public client-side Supabase credentials should be exposed in the frontend. Secret keys must remain server-side.

### Local Development Command

```bash
npm install
npm run dev
```

The application will be accessible through the configured local Vite development address.

